course: dictionary
lesson: 11305
title: Yeah, and when to say yes
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: «Yeah» means yes, but it is a casual word. You hear it with friends, at home and in chats. In school writing and exams, use yes instead.
explain: Tone matters. Said with a smile, «yeah» means agreement. Said in a flat voice, with the eyes rolling, it can mean the opposite. Listen to how it is said as well as what it says.
explain: Context gives the clue. «Oh yeah, I've ONLY told you a million times» is not a yes at all. The speaker is cross and exaggerating, and the word «yeah» adds the sarcasm. Check the words around it, then ask: does this sound like agreement, or like doubt?
fact: Yeah is an adverb and an informal interjection, which means it is casual speech.
fact: Yeah means yes, and it can also show you are listening or agree.
fact: «Yeah, right» is sarcastic and means I don't believe that.
fact: In Australia, «yeah nah» means no, and «nah yeah» means yes.
fact: Yeah is not used in formal writing or exams, so use yes instead.
exercise: «Yeah, I'll be there at six.» What does yeah mean here? | No | *Yes | Maybe later | Goodbye
exercise: When Ana nods and says «yeah» while you explain your idea, what is she showing? | That she is leaving the room | That she is falling asleep | *That she is listening and agrees | That she is angry with you
exercise: Tom says he finished all his homework in ten minutes. Lily says, «Yeah, right.» What does she mean? | *I don't believe you | I am very happy for you | I completely agree with you | I am confused by the homework
test: Which word is best in a formal school essay? | *Yes | Yeah | Uh-huh | Yep
test: «Oh yeah, I've ONLY told you a million times.» What does the speaker mean? | They are agreeing politely | They have lost count of the times they said it | *It is a lot of times, and the speaker is cross | They have only said it once
exam: Which is the best way to answer a formal question in an exam? | Yeah, I think so | *Yes, I think so | Uh-huh, that's right | Yep, sure thing
